<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R78003> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/hasContent> "In various disciplines, initial, mostly unsystematic approaches exist to better organize and make accessible the knowledge \"hidden\" in publications:\n* [Papers-with-Code](https://paperswithcode.com) is a service from Facebook AI that collects research papers (especially algorithms) in the field of artificial intelligence in a structured way according to the scheme task-metric-benchmark and creates rankings from them.\n* [Hi-Knowledge](https://hi-knowledge.org/) is an interactive visualization tool that structures scientific knowledge on invasion biology from more than 1100 publications into a network of 12 invasion hypotheses.\n* [Cooperation Databank (CoDa)](https://cooperationdatabank.org) is a machine-readable history of cooperation research for searching and selecting studies for on-demand meta-analysis.\n* [Energy in Buildings and Communities Programme (IEA-EBC)](https://annex79.iea-ebc.org) extracts structured data relevant to Occupant-Centric Building Design and Operation from the literature and uses the Open Science Framework (OSF) to organize and share the extracted data as Excel documents."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
