<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R78286> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In this study, rhizosphere soil and root tissues of reed canary grass (Phalaris arundinacea), channel grass (Vallisneria spiralis), blackberry (Rubus fructicosus) and goat willow (Salix caprea) were collected from the former Shell and Imperial Industries (ICI) Refinery site in Lancaster, UK. The rates and extents of 14C\u2013hydrocarbons (naphthalene, phenanthrene, hexadecane or octacosane) mineralisation in artificially spiked soils were monitored in the absence and presence of 5% (wet weight) of rhizosphere soil or root tissues. Respirometric and microbial assays were monitored in fresh (0 d) and pre\u2013incubated (28 d) artificially spiked soils following amendment with rhizosphere soil or root tissues. "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
