<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789554> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Crop monitoring using Landsat 8 involves utilizing its multispectral bands from the Operational Land Imager (OLI) and Thermal Infrared Sensor (TIRS) to assess crop health, growth stages, and stress factors. Key indices like NDVI (Normalized Difference Vegetation Index) are derived from the red and near-infrared bands, helping to analyze vegetation vigor. The SWIR bands provide insights into soil moisture and plant water stress, while thermal data aids in evaluating land surface temperature for irrigation management. Landsat 8's high temporal resolution supports long-term monitoring and precision agriculture practices."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
