<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789559> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Crop classification for periodic crop maps involves using remote sensing techniques to identify and map different crop types at specific time intervals throughout a growing season. This process typically leverages satellite or aerial imagery combined with machine learning algorithms to classify the land cover based on spectral characteristics such as vegetation indices, reflectance, and temporal patterns of crop growth. By monitoring crops periodically, it is possible to generate maps that reflect changes in crop type, growth stages, and yield predictions over time. These maps are valuable for agricultural monitoring, land use planning, and decision-making in farming practices, as they provide insights into crop distribution, health, and potential risks."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789559> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789559> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Crop classification for periodic crop maps"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789560> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789560> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Fast Intensity Hue Saturation"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789561> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Phenological profiles in remote sensing refer to the use of satellite or airborne sensors to monitor and analyze the timing of seasonal events in plant and animal life cycles, such as flowering, leafing, and migration. These profiles are critical for understanding ecological patterns and climate impacts, as they help track how environmental changes influence biological processes over time. By capturing data on vegetation indices, temperature, and precipitation, remote sensing allows for large-scale, real-time monitoring of phenological events, providing insights into ecosystem health, crop performance, and the effects of climate change."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789561> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789561> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Phenological profiles"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
