<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789563> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Soil texture estimation from Landsat 8 OLI data involves using the satellite's multispectral bands (such as visible, near-infrared, and shortwave infrared) to analyze the reflectance properties of soil. By calculating spectral indices like NDVI and NDSI, researchers can distinguish soil from vegetation and assess its texture (sand, silt, clay). Machine learning models or empirical relationships are often applied to correlate spectral data with soil properties, enabling the creation of soil texture maps."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
