<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789570> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Advancements in Remote Sensing with Landsat-8: Crop Monitoring, Soil Estimation, and Environmental Analysis"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789572> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Crop classification for periodic crop maps using Landsat 8 involves analyzing the satellite's multispectral imagery to identify and categorize different crop types over time. Landsat 8 provides high-resolution data across multiple spectral bands, including visible, near-infrared (NIR), and shortwave infrared (SWIR), which are particularly useful for distinguishing between various crops based on their unique spectral signatures. By using vegetation indices like NDVI, combined with machine learning algorithms such as Random Forest or Support Vector Machines, periodic crop maps can be generated. These maps track crop growth stages and types throughout the season, enabling agricultural monitoring, yield prediction, and land use management."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789572> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
