<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789588> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Object-Based Analysis (OBA) for coral reef mapping involves segmenting high-resolution satellite or aerial imagery into distinct objects or regions that represent homogeneous areas, rather than classifying individual pixels. In this approach, spectral, spatial, and contextual information (such as shape, texture, and size) are used to identify and classify coral reef areas, surrounding waters, and other marine features. The process typically involves steps like image segmentation, feature extraction, and classification using machine learning algorithms or rule-based methods. OBA is effective for mapping coral reefs because it helps distinguish complex features like coral cover, seagrass, and algae, improving the accuracy of reef monitoring and ecosystem health assessment."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789588> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789588> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Object based anlaysis for Coral reef mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789589> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Object-Based Analysis (OBA) is a remote sensing technique that focuses on classifying and analyzing objects or regions within an image, rather than individual pixels. In OBA, images are first segmented into meaningful, homogeneous regions or objects based on characteristics such as color, texture, shape, and spatial relationships. These objects are then classified using machine learning algorithms or rule-based methods. OBA is particularly effective for high-resolution imagery, where pixels may not accurately represent real-world features."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789589> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789589> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Object based anlaysis"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
