<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789633> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "While traditional Fisher Discriminant Analysis works by finding a linear projection that maximizes the separation between classes based on their means and variances, the Kernel Fisher Discriminant uses a kernel function (e.g., Gaussian, polynomial) to implicitly map the data into a higher-dimensional space. In this transformed space, the algorithm seeks the optimal linear projection for class separation, even when the classes are not linearly separable in the original feature space."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789633> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
