<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789704> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Coal-bed methane (CBM) exploration using hyperspectral imaging (HSI) involves the use of hyperspectral data to detect and assess the potential for methane gas trapped in coal seams. Hyperspectral sensors capture detailed spectral information across a wide range of wavelengths, which can help identify surface features indicative of CBM presence, such as vegetation stress or gas seepage. By analyzing specific spectral bands, such as those in the shortwave infrared, HSI can detect changes in soil and vegetation caused by methane emissions."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789704> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789704> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coal-bed methane exploration from HSI"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789705> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Hydrocarbon mapping uses remote sensing techniques to detect and monitor petroleum and natural gas deposits on land or at sea. Satellite imagery and aerial sensors, such as multispectral, hyperspectral, and thermal infrared data, are employed to identify features linked to hydrocarbons, such as oil spills, gas flares, and surface anomalies. Techniques like spectral indices (e.g., NDVI), thermal infrared imaging, and Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) are commonly used to identify signs of contamination, surface changes, or emissions."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789705> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789705> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Hydrocarbon mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789706> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Qinshui Basin is a major coal-producing region located in Shanxi Province, China, known for its rich coal-bed methane (CBM) resources. It is one of the largest CBM reserves in China and plays a key role in the country's energy production. The basin has significant potential for both coal and natural gas extraction, with CBM being an important energy source due to its cleaner burning properties compared to traditional coal."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789706> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789706> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Qinshui Basin"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789707> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Normalized Hydrocarbon Index (NHI) is a spectral index used in remote sensing to detect the presence of hydrocarbons, particularly oil and gas, on the Earth's surface. It is derived by analyzing specific spectral bands that are sensitive to hydrocarbons, typically in the visible and infrared regions of the electromagnetic spectrum. The NHI is calculated by normalizing the difference between spectral bands that are sensitive to hydrocarbon features, such as the near-infrared and shortwave infrared bands"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789707> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789707> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Normalized Hydrocarbon Index (NHI)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789708> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Jincheng Coal Mining Area is a significant coal mining region located in Shanxi Province, China. It is known for its large reserves of coal, which have made it a major center for coal production in the country. The area has extensive underground and open-pit mining operations, contributing substantially to China's energy supply. However, the region also faces environmental challenges, including land degradation, water contamination, and air pollution due to mining activities. Remote sensing technologies are often used to monitor land cover changes, subsidence, and environmental impacts in the Jincheng Coal Mining Area, helping in sustainable management and rehabilitation efforts."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
