<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789712> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Hyperspectral imagery (HSI) is increasingly used in oil and gas exploration to identify and monitor potential resources and environmental impacts. HSI captures data across many narrow spectral bands, allowing for the detection of specific spectral signatures associated with hydrocarbons, such as oil and gas seeps on the surface. By analyzing these spectral signatures, HSI can help detect features like oil slicks, gas flares, and vegetation stress due to hydrocarbon contamination. It also aids in mapping surface features, monitoring land use changes, and assessing environmental risks."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789712> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789712> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "hyperspectral image for oil and gas exploration"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789713> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Yulin Gas Field is a significant natural gas field located in the Ordos Basin in Shanxi Province, China. It is one of the largest gas fields in China, primarily producing coalbed methane (CBM), a type of natural gas found in coal seams. The field plays a key role in China's efforts to diversify its energy sources and reduce reliance on coal. Remote sensing technologies, including satellite imagery and hyperspectral data, are used to monitor the environmental impacts of gas extraction in the region, such as land subsidence, vegetation stress, and methane emissions."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
