<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789725> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "This collection of studies examines the diverse applications of hyperspectral remote sensing for natural resource exploration and agricultural monitoring. Topics include coal-bed methane exploration, oil and gas microseepage detection, and the comparison of new-generation hyperspectral sensors like DESIS and PRISMA with traditional multispectral data for global agriculture studies. The research presents advanced spectral techniques, such as Z-score distance for classification and endmember extraction from Hyperion, offering valuable tools for researchers, remote sensing professionals, and students."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
