<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789764> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Pan sharpening can be decomposed into two separate resources: 'Pan' and 'Sharpening'. The term 'Pan' might refer to the panchromatic band in remote sensing, which captures a broad spectrum of light. 'Sharpening' could refer to the process of enhancing the spatial resolution of an image by merging high-resolution panchromatic and lower resolution multispectral image bands."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789764> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Problem> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789764> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789764> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pan sharpening"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789765> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Fusion of hyperspectral data with panchromatic data combines the high spectral resolution of hyperspectral imagery with the high spatial resolution of panchromatic imagery. This process enhances both the spectral detail and spatial clarity, improving classification accuracy and object detection in remote sensing applications, such as land cover mapping and resource monitoring."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789765> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Problem> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789765> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789765> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fusion of hyperpscetral data with panchromatic data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789766> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "This technique is a method for the fusion of hyperspectral and panchromatic images. It uses the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to combine the high spectral resolution of hyperspectral data with the high spatial resolution of panchromatic data. It is useful in improving the spatial detail of hyperspectral images while maintaining the spectral information."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789766> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789766> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gram Schmidt mode 1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
