<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789785> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Construction material mapping using Hyperspectral Imaging (HSI) involves using hyperspectral sensors to detect and classify various materials in construction sites or buildings. HSI captures a wide range of spectral bands, allowing for detailed analysis of surface materials like concrete, asphalt, wood, metals, and ceramics. By analyzing the unique spectral signatures of these materials, HSI can help identify and map construction materials, assess their condition, and monitor changes over time. This technique is useful in urban planning, infrastructure maintenance, and assessing building materials' properties, such as moisture content or degradation, without the need for direct sampling or invasive methods."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
