<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789786> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "This collection of studies explores the diverse applications of hyperspectral remote sensing in vegetation management, resource mapping, and agricultural monitoring. Topics include vegetation management by Catchment Management Authorities using Hyperion imagery, uranium mapping, leaf nitrogen assessment, and comparisons of new-generation hyperspectral sensors like ISS DESIS with traditional multispectral data. The research introduces advanced techniques for hyperspectral pansharpening and component substitution, offering valuable insights and methodologies for researchers, remote sensing professionals, and students in environmental management, resource exploration, and precision agriculture."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
