<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789794> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Relative Chlorophyll Content (SPAD value) refers to a measure of chlorophyll concentration in plant leaves, commonly obtained using a SPAD meter. The SPAD value is a numerical index that correlates with the chlorophyll content, providing a quick, non-destructive method to assess plant health. This value is widely used in agriculture to monitor crop vitality, predict yield, and optimize fertilization practices by assessing chlorophyll levels, which are directly related to photosynthetic efficiency."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789794> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789794> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " relative chlorophyll content (SPAD value)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789795> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The PSR3500 spectrograph is a high-resolution, portable, and versatile spectrometer used for analyzing a wide range of materials across the visible, near-infrared, and shortwave infrared spectra. It is commonly used in remote sensing, environmental monitoring, and material identification. The PSR3500 provides detailed spectral data, allowing for precise identification of substances based on their unique spectral signatures. This device is useful in fields like agriculture, geology, and food quality control, where accurate and non-destructive material analysis is required."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789795> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
