<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789813> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Hyperspectral Imaging (HSI) is highly effective for detecting invasive species by capturing detailed spectral information across a wide range of wavelengths. Each plant species, including invasive ones, has a unique spectral signature due to differences in their chemical composition, leaf structure, and pigments. HSI can identify these signatures, allowing for the detection and mapping of invasive species in ecosystems."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
