<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789825> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Snow properties from hyperspectral data can be assessed by analyzing the spectral characteristics of snow-covered areas across various wavelengths. Hyperspectral imagery, with its high spectral resolution, allows for the detailed examination of snow parameters such as snow grain size, snow albedo, snow depth, and snow water equivalent (SWE). These properties affect how snow reflects and absorbs light, particularly in the visible and infrared regions."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789825> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789825> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Snow Properties from hyperspectral data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789826> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Snow parameters refer to various physical and spectral characteristics used to analyze and monitor snow cover in remote sensing applications. These parameters include snow depth, snow water equivalent (SWE), snow albedo, snow grain size, and snow temperature."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789826> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789826> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Snow parameters"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789827> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789827> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Italian Alps"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789828> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Meteo I/O meteorological model is a tool used to simulate and analyze atmospheric conditions for various applications, including environmental monitoring, climate studies, and agricultural management. It integrates meteorological data such as temperature, humidity, wind speed, and precipitation to predict weather patterns and their effects on different ecosystems."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789828> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789828> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Meteo I/O meteorological model"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789829> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The BIOSNICAR model is a biogeochemical model designed to simulate and assess the interactions between vegetation, soil, and the atmosphere in terrestrial ecosystems. It focuses on the cycling of carbon, nitrogen, and other nutrients, helping to understand ecosystem dynamics and their responses to environmental changes. BIOSNICAR is often used for modeling plant growth, carbon sequestration, and nutrient cycling in various landscapes."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789829> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
