<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789853> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P15411> "ATCOR 4 is a sophisticated atmospheric correction software used in remote sensing to process and correct images for atmospheric effects, such as scattering and absorption, that can distort the data collected by sensors. It is commonly applied to multispectral and hyperspectral satellite images. ATCOR 4 uses radiative transfer models to simulate the atmosphere's impact on the sensor data and then adjusts the image to reflect the true surface properties. This correction improves the accuracy of image analysis for applications like vegetation monitoring, land use classification, and environmental change detection by removing atmospheric interference."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
