<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789889> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Mapping vegetation biodiversity using hyperspectral data involves using the detailed spectral information captured by hyperspectral sensors to identify and classify different plant species and vegetation types across large areas. Hyperspectral data provides high-resolution spectral bands, which capture unique reflectance features of vegetation related to species composition, leaf structure, and health. By analyzing these spectral signatures, it is possible to create biodiversity maps that show the distribution of various plant species and monitor changes in vegetation diversity over time."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789889> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
