<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789891> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "National Parks in Italy are protected natural areas established to conserve biodiversity, preserve natural landscapes, and provide recreational opportunities. Italy is home to numerous national parks, such as the Gran Paradiso National Park, the Cinque Terre National Park, and the Pollino National Park, each offering unique ecosystems, wildlife, and natural beauty. These parks are vital for preserving Italy's diverse flora and fauna, including many endemic species. They also play a significant role in environmental research and tourism, attracting visitors for activities like hiking, wildlife watching, and cultural exploration."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789891> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
