<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789892> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "A Convolutional Autoencoder (CAE) is a type of neural network used for unsupervised learning tasks, such as data compression, noise reduction, and feature extraction. It combines convolutional layers with the autoencoder architecture to learn efficient representations of input data. The network consists of an encoder that compresses the input into a lower-dimensional latent space and a decoder that reconstructs the original data from this compressed representation. CAEs are particularly effective in image processing tasks, as the convolutional layers capture spatial hierarchies and patterns in the data, making them suitable for applications like image denoising, anomaly detection, and dimensionality reduction in remote sensing and computer vision."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789892> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
