<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789896> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Urban land classification using hyperspectral data involves analyzing the detailed spectral information from hyperspectral sensors to identify and map various land cover types within urban environments. Hyperspectral data provides high spectral resolution across many bands, enabling the detection of subtle differences between materials like buildings, roads, vegetation, and water bodies. This allows for more accurate and detailed classification compared to traditional multispectral data."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
