<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789904> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Satellite data quality refers to the accuracy, reliability, and consistency of data collected from satellites. It encompasses several factors, including spatial, spectral, and temporal resolution, as well as the sensor's calibration, atmospheric conditions, and potential sources of error such as noise or distortion. High-quality satellite data is essential for accurate remote sensing analysis, including land cover classification, environmental monitoring, and climate studies."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
