<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789912> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The coefficient of correlation (r\u00B2), also known as the coefficient of determination, is a statistical measure that indicates the proportion of the variance in the dependent variable that can be explained by the independent variable(s) in a regression model. R\u00B2 ranges from 0 to 1, with a value closer to 1 suggesting a strong relationship between the variables, while a value closer to 0 indicates a weak relationship. It is widely used in various fields, including remote sensing, to assess the goodness of fit of models, such as in land classification, vegetation studies, and predicting environmental changes."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
