<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789944> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Hyperspectral data for vegetation mapping involves using high-resolution spectral information from hyperspectral sensors to classify and analyze vegetation types based on their unique spectral reflectance characteristics. Hyperspectral sensors capture data across hundreds of narrow spectral bands, enabling the detection of subtle differences in plant properties, such as leaf pigment, moisture content, and health."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789944> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789944> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hyperpsectral data for vegetation mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789945> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Non-Photosynthetic Vegetation (NPV) mapping involves identifying and mapping vegetation that does not actively participate in photosynthesis, such as dead or senescent plants, plant litter, or non-vegetated areas like bare soil. Remote sensing, especially using multispectral and hyperspectral data, can be used to distinguish NPV from photosynthetically active vegetation by analyzing specific spectral features."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789945> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789945> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Non-Photosynthetic Vegetation (NPV)  mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789946> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
