<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789947> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "EnHyR (Environmental Hyperspectral Reflectance) Workflow refers to a systematic approach used for processing and analyzing hyperspectral data to study environmental factors and their impacts. This workflow typically involves several key steps:\n\nData Acquisition: Collecting hyperspectral images or reflectance data through sensors mounted on satellites, aircraft, or drones.\nPreprocessing: Correcting the data for atmospheric effects, sensor calibration, and geometric distortions to ensure accuracy.\nSpectral Analysis: Extracting spectral features or indices from the data to highlight specific environmental properties such as vegetation health, soil moisture, or water quality.\nClassification or Mapping: Applying classification algorithms (e.g., machine learning) to categorize land cover, vegetation types, or monitor environmental changes.\nValidation: Comparing the results with ground-truth data or other reference sources to assess the accuracy of the analysis.\nThe EnHyR workflow is widely used for applications like vegetation mapping, land monitoring, and environmental impact assessments, providing detailed insights into ecosystem health and changes."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789947> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789947> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " EnHyR Workflow"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
