<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789951> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Deforestation mapping using hyperspectral data involves analyzing the detailed spectral information provided by hyperspectral sensors to detect and monitor changes in forest cover, particularly the loss of trees due to deforestation. Hyperspectral data, with its wide range of spectral bands, allows for the identification of subtle changes in vegetation health, species composition, and land use."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789951> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789951> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Deforestation mapping using hyperspectral data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789952> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Forest mapping involves using remote sensing data, such as satellite or airborne imagery, to identify, classify, and monitor forested areas. This process helps in mapping forest boundaries, types, health, and biomass. Hyperspectral, multispectral, and LiDAR data are commonly used for forest mapping, as they provide detailed information about vegetation types, forest structure, and canopy characteristics."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789952> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789952> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Forest mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789953> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Brazilian Amazon Forest is the largest tropical rainforest in the world, spanning approximately 5.5 million square kilometers across Brazil and several other South American countries. It is a critical ecosystem for biodiversity, carbon storage, and climate regulation. The forest is home to a vast array of plant and animal species, many of which are unique to the region. However, the Brazilian Amazon faces significant threats from deforestation due to agriculture, logging, and infrastructure development. Remote sensing technologies, including hyperspectral and multispectral satellite imagery, are frequently used to monitor changes in forest cover, assess deforestation rates, and support conservation efforts to protect this vital ecological resource."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789953> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789953> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Brazilian Amazon Forest"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789954> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "A One-Dimensional Convolutional Neural Network (1D-CNN) is a type of deep learning model that uses convolutional layers to process and analyze sequential or temporal data. Unlike traditional 2D CNNs used for image processing, 1D-CNNs are designed for data with a single spatial dimension, such as time series, audio signals, or other types of sequential data. The model applies convolutional filters across the input data to extract features, followed by pooling layers and fully connected layers for classification or regression tasks. 1D-CNNs are particularly useful for applications like speech recognition, sensor data analysis, and sequence prediction, where patterns and dependencies over time are important."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789954> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789954> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " One dimensional convolutional neural network (1D-CNN)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
