<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789958> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Methane estimation from hyperspectral data involves analyzing the spectral signatures captured by hyperspectral sensors to detect and quantify methane gas in the atmosphere. Hyperspectral sensors can capture detailed spectral information across many narrow bands, particularly in the infrared region, where methane has unique absorption features. By analyzing these spectral bands, algorithms can identify methane plumes and estimate their concentration. This technique is particularly useful in detecting methane emissions from various sources like landfills, oil and gas facilities, and wetlands."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789958> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789958> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Methane estimation from hyperpsectral data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789959> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Methane mapping involves using remote sensing techniques, particularly satellite or airborne sensors, to detect and monitor methane gas emissions in the atmosphere. Methane, a potent greenhouse gas, is often mapped to track sources such as oil and gas operations, landfills, agricultural activities, and natural sources like wetlands. Hyperspectral, multispectral, and specialized sensors like those on NASA's GHGSat or the Sentinel-5P satellite, can capture methane's unique spectral signature in the infrared spectrum."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789959> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789959> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Methane mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789960> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789960> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Turkmenistan"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789961> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789961> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " DN to radiance"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789962> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "MAG1C (Matched filter with Albedo correction and reweighted L1 sparsity Code) is an advanced algorithm designed for hyperspectral data analysis. It combines a matched filtering technique with an albedo correction and a reweighted L1 sparsity method to improve the accuracy of identifying and quantifying materials or features in hyperspectral images.\n\nThe matched filter is used to enhance the detection of specific materials by maximizing the signal-to-noise ratio based on known spectral signatures.\nAlbedo correction compensates for the variations in surface reflectance caused by the angle of illumination and surface properties, ensuring more accurate material identification.\nReweighted L1 sparsity is a regularization technique that promotes sparsity in the solution, helping to focus on key features while reducing noise and irrelevant data."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789962> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789962> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " MAG1C (Matched filter with Albedo correction and reweighted L1 sparsity Code)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
