<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789975> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Snow grain size mapping from satellite data involves using remote sensing technologies to estimate the size of snow grains in snowpacks, which influences the reflectance properties of snow. Grain size affects the snow's optical characteristics, such as albedo, and can be used to assess snowmelt dynamics, climate conditions, and hydrological models."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789975> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789975> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Snow grain size mapping form satellite data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789976> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Grain size mapping involves using remote sensing data, often from hyperspectral or multispectral imagery, to determine and classify the grain size distribution of surface materials, such as soil, sand, or rocks. This process helps in identifying different sediment types based on their spectral signatures, which vary according to the particle size, composition, and texture. In the context of hyperspectral data, specific spectral bands are sensitive to the reflectance characteristics of materials with different grain sizes."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789976> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789976> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Grain size mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789977> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789977> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " South Lhonak glacier"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789978> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789978> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " SID"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789979> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Band area refers to the area under a specific spectral band or range of wavelengths in remote sensing data. In the context of hyperspectral or multispectral imagery, each band represents a particular portion of the electromagnetic spectrum, capturing unique information about the Earth's surface. The \"area\" under a band is often used to describe the strength of reflectance or absorption within that spectral range, which can be important for identifying specific materials, land cover types, or environmental conditions. In certain applications, such as vegetation analysis or mineral mapping, the area under a spectral band (or a set of bands) can be used to extract meaningful information about the composition or properties of the surface being studied."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789979> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
