<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789993> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Monitoring of water biophysical parameters involves tracking key characteristics of aquatic environments that influence biological and physical processes in water bodies. These parameters typically include water temperature, turbidity, salinity, dissolved oxygen, chlorophyll-a concentration, and suspended particulate matter. Remote sensing technologies, such as satellite and drone-based sensors, are commonly used to measure these parameters, providing spatially extensive and frequent data for large bodies of water."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789993> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789993> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "monitoring of water biophysical parameters"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789994> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Remote sensing techniques, such as satellite imagery, are commonly used to monitor the health of aquatic ecosystems by analyzing parameters like water quality, vegetation coverage, and changes in habitat."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789994> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789994> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Aquatic Ecosystems"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789995> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789995> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Garda lake"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789996> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Lake Trasimeno is the largest lake in central Italy, located in the Umbria region. It covers an area of about 128 square kilometers and is known for its scenic beauty, rich biodiversity, and historical significance. The lake is a shallow body of water, with a maximum depth of about 6 meters, and is surrounded by hills and picturesque towns. It is an important habitat for various species of birds, fish, and aquatic plants."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789996> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789996> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Trasimeno lake"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789997> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "he North Adriatic Sea is the northernmost part of the Adriatic Sea, bordered by Italy to the west, Slovenia to the north, and Croatia to the east. It is characterized by shallow waters, with varying depths and significant tidal influences. The region is important for both ecological and economic reasons, supporting rich biodiversity and playing a critical role in local fisheries, tourism, and shipping industries. The North Adriatic Sea is also known for its complex hydrodynamic processes, influenced by river inflows such as the Po River, which contribute to its unique water quality and sediment characteristics. Monitoring of environmental parameters like water quality, temperature, and chlorophyll-a concentration in this area is crucial for managing coastal ecosystems, preserving marine biodiversity, and addressing pollution threats."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789997> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789997> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " North Adriatic sea"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789998> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Mixture Density Network (MDN) is a type of machine learning algorithm that combines neural networks with mixture models to predict probability distributions instead of point estimates. It is particularly useful for tasks where there is inherent uncertainty or multi-modal outputs, such as regression problems with complex, non-linear relationships. An MDN consists of a neural network that outputs the parameters (means, variances, and mixing coefficients) of a mixture of Gaussian distributions, rather than a single value. These parameters define the probability distribution of possible outcomes. The MDN can model multiple possible outcomes for a given input, making it suitable for applications like uncertainty quantification, prediction of complex systems, and generative modeling."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789998> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789998> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Mixture Density Network (MDN) machine learning algorithm"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789999> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "WISPstation is a wireless sensor platform designed for environmental monitoring, often used in remote sensing applications. It typically includes a combination of sensors that can measure various environmental parameters such as temperature, humidity, air quality, and radiation, and can be integrated with other sensor types like those for measuring water quality or soil conditions. WISPstation is commonly used for applications such as atmospheric monitoring, agricultural monitoring, and forest management."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789999> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R789999> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " WISPstation"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
