<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790004> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Spline interpolation is a mathematical method used to construct a smooth curve that passes through a given set of data points. It uses piecewise polynomial functions, called splines, to ensure a smooth transition between points. The most common type is the cubic spline, which fits a cubic polynomial between each pair of data points and ensures that the first and second derivatives of the polynomials are continuous across the data points."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
