<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790030> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "A comprehensive survey and exploration of small language models (SLM), techniques, applications, and trustworthiness in the era of LLMs"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Small Language Models (SLMs) survey"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790031> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The GQA (Grouped Query Attention) mechanism is a variation of the traditional Multi-Head Attention (MHA) used in Transformer models. \u200B In GQA, the attention heads are grouped to share query representations while keeping key and value representations separate.\u200B It reduces computational complexity and memory usage while maintaining the model's ability to capture diverse aspects of the input data. \u200BGQA allows multiple attention heads to use the same query vectors."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GQA"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790032> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The SiLU (Sigmoid Linear Unit) activation function is defined as: SiLU(x) = x * sigmoid(x). It effectively combines the sigmoid function with its input, enhancing modeling capabilities. It is computationally efficient and introduces no extra parameters, making it a preferred choice in SLMs."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SiLU"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790033> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Shared Embedding: A technique where the same embedding weights are used for both input and output layers, making the model more efficient and compact. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Shared Embedding"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790034> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Pruning: The process of removing less critical parameters to reduce model size and computational requirements while maintaining performance. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pruning"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790035> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Distillation: A method where a smaller model (student) is trained to mimic the outputs of a larger model (teacher), retaining much of the teacher\u2019s capabilities with fewer parameters. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790035> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790035> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Distillation"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790036> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback): A technique that involves gathering human-preferred data, training a reward model, and fine-tuning the language model using reinforcement learning to align it with human preferences. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790036> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RLHF"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790037> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Sentinel-2, part of the European Space Agency's Copernicus program, is highly effective for water quality monitoring due to its high-resolution multispectral imagery. It provides frequent, global coverage with a spatial resolution of 10 to 60 meters and operates in 13 spectral bands, ranging from visible to shortwave infrared wavelengths. This capability allows for the detection of water quality indicators like chlorophyll-a concentration, turbidity, suspended sediments, and the presence of harmful algal blooms (HABs)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790037> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790037> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sentinel 2 for water quality monitoring"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790038> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "In terms of remote sensing, water quality can be monitored using satellite and airborne sensors that detect various water properties from a distance. Remote sensing technologies, such as multispectral and hyperspectral imaging, enable the detection of water parameters like turbidity, chlorophyll concentration, temperature, and the presence of pollutants (e.g., oils, heavy metals, or suspended sediments)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Water quality"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790039> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The San Roque Reservoir in Argentina is located in the province of C\u00F3rdoba and is one of the most prominent artificial reservoirs in the region. \n\nLocation and Formation: It is situated near the city of Villa Carlos Paz, created by the San Roque Dam, which was first constructed in the late 19th century and later reconstructed in the mid-20th century."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790039> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790039> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " San Roque Reservoir, Argentina"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790040> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Rejection Sampling (RS) training technique involves generating multiple candidate outputs and selecting the best one based on a predefined criterion to improve the quality and reliability of the model's responses."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RS"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
