<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790044> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Fractional Cover Estimation using Sentinel-2 data is an important method for assessing the distribution of vegetation, bare soil, and non-photosynthetic vegetation (NPV) in a given area. This method is widely used in land cover classification, vegetation monitoring, and ecological studies. Sentinel-2, with its high spatial resolution (10\u201360 meters) and 13 spectral bands, provides the necessary data to estimate these fractions effectively."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790044> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790044> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fractional Cover Estimation for Sentinel 2 data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790045> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Roorkee"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790046> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Fractional Vegetation Cover (FVC) is a key index used to quantify the proportion of a pixel covered by vegetation. It helps in assessing the health and density of vegetation and is widely used in environmental monitoring, land cover classification, and vegetation studies. FVC represents the fraction of a pixel that is covered by green vegetation, and it can be estimated using remote sensing data, such as that from Sentinel-2, which provides high-resolution multispectral imagery."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790046> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790046> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Fractional vegettaion indices (FVC)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
