<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790050> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Soil salinity mapping using hyperspectral imagery involves utilizing the detailed spectral information across hundreds of narrow bands to detect and quantify soil salinity levels. Hyperspectral sensors provide high spectral resolution, allowing for more precise identification of the unique reflectance patterns associated with salt-affected soils, particularly in the shortwave infrared (SWIR) region. By analyzing specific spectral bands sensitive to salt presence, such as those in the SWIR and visible regions, soil salinity can be mapped accurately."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790050> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790050> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Soil Salinity mapping using hyperspectral image"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790051> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Soil salinity mapping is an important process for monitoring and managing soil health, particularly in agricultural and arid regions where salinization can have a significant impact on crop production and ecosystems. Soil salinity refers to the concentration of soluble salts in the soil, and excessive salinity can hinder plant growth, reduce agricultural productivity, and lead to land degradation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790051> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Soil Salinity mapping"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790052> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Masonite Road Fire occurred near Newcastle, New South Wales, in January 2018. The fire burned approximately 2,300 hectares (around 5,683 acres) and caused significant smoke that impacted visibility, temporarily closing Newcastle Airport. Firefighting operations included the use of a DC-10 air tanker, which dropped water and fire retardants to assist ground crews in controlling the fire.\n\nAuthorities conducted backburning near the northern side of the airport as part of their firefighting strategy, and roads such as Richardson Road were intermittently reopened as conditions improved. This fire exemplified the challenges of fighting wildfires in proximity to populated areas and critical infrastructure"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790052> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790052> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Masonite Road Fire, Newcastle"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790053> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Blue Mountains, Sydney"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790054> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P15411> "https://www.earthdatascience.org/courses/earth-analytics/multispectral-remote-sensing-modis/normalized-burn-index-dNBR/"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790054> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Differenced Normalized Burn Ratio (dNBR) is a remote sensing index widely used to assess the impact of wildfires on vegetation and soil. It measures the change in reflectance before and after a fire by comparing the Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR) calculated from satellite imagery."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790054> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " dNBR (Differenced Normalized Burn Ratio)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790055> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Interferometric Coherence Analysis is a technique used in synthetic aperture radar (SAR) interferometry to measure the correlation between two SAR images acquired over the same area at different times, viewing angles, or polarization modes. The coherence values, ranging between 0 and 1, indicate the quality of the interferometric phase and provide insights into surface changes or stability."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790055> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Interferometric Coherence Analysis"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790056> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Sequential Forward Selection (SFS) is a feature selection technique used in machine learning and statistics to identify the subset of features that most improve the performance of a model. SFS is particularly useful when working with datasets that contain many variables, some of which may be irrelevant or redundant."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Sequential Forward Selection (SFS)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
