<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790068> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Multi-Head Attention (MHA) mechanism is a core component of the Transformer architecture, designed to capture different aspects of the input data by using multiple attention heads. \u200B Each head independently performs scaled dot-product attention, and their outputs are concatenated and linearly transformed to produce the final result"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790068> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
