<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790069> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "mountain range in New South Wales"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790069> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Blue Mountains"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790070> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The SwiGLU (Swish-Gated Linear Units) activation function integrates the Swish activation function with Gated Linear Units. \u200B It is defined as: SwiGLU(x) = Swish(x * W + b) \u2299 (x * V + c) \u200Bwhere: W and V are weight matrices, b and c are bias terms, Swish(x) = x * sigmoid(x). This combination enhances expressiveness and computational efficiency, making it a preferred choice in advanced models."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790070> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790070> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790070> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SwiGLU"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790071> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "RoPE (Rotary Positional Embedding): A positional encoding method that introduces a rotational matrix to the embeddings, enhancing the model\u2019s capacity for understanding the relative positions of tokens within a sequence. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790071> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790071> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RoPE"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790072> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "RMSNorm (Root Mean Square Layer Normalization): A normalization technique that stabilizes the training process by normalizing layer outputs, accelerating convergence, and reducing computational demands. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790072> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RMSNorm"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790073> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Radar Intensity Difference refers to the change in backscattered radar signal intensity between two or more SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) images over the same area. It is often used in remote sensing to detect and analyze surface changes, including land cover changes, natural disasters, or human activity."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790073> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790073> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Radar Intensity Difference"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790074> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P26> "10.48366/R790074"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
