<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790081> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The SwiGLU (Swish-Gated Linear Units) activation function integrates the Swish activation function with Gated Linear Units. \u200B It is defined as: SwiGLU(x) = Swish(x * W + b) \u2299 (x * V + c) \u200Bwhere: W and V are weight matrices, b and c are bias terms, Swish(x) = x * sigmoid(x). This combination enhances expressiveness and computational efficiency, making it a preferred choice in advanced models."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
