<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790101> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Neural network-based crop classification involves using deep learning models, typically convolutional neural networks (CNNs), to automatically identify and classify different crop types from satellite imagery or remote sensing data. These models are trained on labeled data, such as Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 satellite images, by learning patterns in the spectral features (e.g., NDVI, texture, and backscatter coefficients) that correspond to specific crop types."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
