<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790137> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Multitemporal analysis involves the examination of satellite or remote sensing data collected over multiple time periods to detect and analyze changes in the Earth's surface. By comparing images or data from different times, this technique helps identify trends, monitor dynamic processes, and assess environmental changes such as land cover changes, urbanization, vegetation growth, deforestation, or disaster impacts."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790137> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
