<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790142> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Land cover analysis using multispectral data involves classifying and mapping different types of land cover on the Earth's surface by utilizing the various spectral bands provided by multispectral satellite imagery, such as from Sentinel-2 or Landsat. These datasets typically capture images in several bands across the visible, near-infrared (NIR), and short-wave infrared (SWIR) regions, each sensitive to specific surface features. T"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790142> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790142> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Land cover analysis using Multispectral data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790143> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P15411> "https://mapasyst.extension.org/remote-sensing-resampling-methods/"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790143> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Spatial resampling is a process used in remote sensing and geospatial analysis to adjust the spatial resolution of raster data, either by increasing or decreasing the pixel size. It is typically necessary when combining datasets with different spatial resolutions or when transforming data to a new coordinate system."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790143> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Spatial resampling"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790144> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "A Deep Convolutional Neural Network (DCNN) is a type of deep learning architecture specifically designed for processing and analyzing visual data, such as images or videos. It is an extension of the basic Convolutional Neural Network (CNN), with multiple layers that enable it to learn hierarchical features from raw data, making it highly effective for tasks like image classification, object detection, and semantic segmentation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790144> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Deep convolutional neural network (CNN)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790145> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Salinas Hyperspectral Dataset is a well-known dataset commonly used for testing and benchmarking algorithms in the field of hyperspectral image classification. It was collected by the Airborne Visible/Infrared Imaging Spectrometer (AVIRIS) over the Salinas Valley, California, and contains 224 spectral bands with a spatial resolution of 3.7 meters, covering a region of agricultural fields. The dataset has a total of 16 classes representing different types of land cover, including various crops like lettuce, broccoli, and grapes, as well as natural features such as water bodies and bare soil."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790145> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Salinas hyperspectral dataset"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
