<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790149> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Fusion of multispectral and aerial images combines the strengths of both types of data to create a more comprehensive and informative image for various applications like land cover mapping, urban planning, and agriculture. Multispectral images, typically captured by satellites like Sentinel-2, provide valuable spectral information across multiple bands (visible, near-infrared, etc.), which helps differentiate between various surface types (e.g., vegetation, water, urban areas)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790149> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fusion of multispectral and Aerial images"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790150> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Image fusion"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790151> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Reykjavik, Iceland"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790152> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The main goal of S2PF is to improve the spatial resolution of Sentinel-2\u2019s lower-resolution bands (such as the 20m and 60m bands) to match the higher-resolution bands (10m). This is typically done by fusing the multispectral information from Sentinel-2 with high-resolution data in a way that maintains the spectral integrity of the original Sentinel-2 image while enhancing the spatial detail.\n\nSteps in S2PF (Sentinel-2 Photo Fusion):\nData Acquisition: Collect Sentinel-2 multispectral data (e.g., with bands like NIR, Red, Green) and high-resolution optical images (e.g., from drones).\n\nPreprocessing: Perform radiometric calibration, geometric alignment, and atmospheric correction on both datasets to ensure consistency.\n\nFusion: The fusion process can be carried out using methods like pansharpening (combining a high-resolution panchromatic image with multispectral bands) or more advanced techniques like Wavelet Transform, Principal Component Analysis (PCA), or deep learning-based fusion methods. These methods aim to merge spatial and spectral information, increasing spatial detail while preserving the spectral characteristics of the Sentinel-2 bands.\n\nPost-Processing: This step may include refining the fused image to eliminate artifacts, adjusting for contrast, and performing accuracy assessment through comparison with ground truth or high-resolution datasets."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790152> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " S2PF (Sentinel-2 Photo Fusion)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
