<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790173> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Forest fire detection using Sentinel-1 (SAR) and Sentinel-2 (multispectral) data is a powerful approach for monitoring and managing wildfires. Each satellite provides unique advantages for detecting fires in various conditions:\n\nSentinel-1 (SAR Data): Sentinel-1, with its Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) capabilities, is highly effective for detecting forest fires, especially in challenging conditions such as smoke or cloud cover. It can detect fire-induced changes in the landscape, such as burn scars, surface roughness, and moisture levels. Sentinel-1 can also identify hotspots during active fires by capturing temperature variations and changes in surface scattering properties.\n\nSentinel-2 (Multispectral Data): Sentinel-2 provides high-resolution optical imagery across multiple spectral bands, including the visible and near-infrared (NIR) spectrum, which is valuable for fire detection and assessment. After a fire, the data can be used to assess burn severity by using indices like the Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR) or Burned Area Index (BAI) to differentiate between burned and unburned areas. Sentinel-2's multispectral data also helps in detecting fire in its early stages by identifying the heat signature or smoke plumes, especially with the use of thermal infrared bands."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790173> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790173> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Forest fire detection from Sentinel and Sentinel 2 data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790174> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790174> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Sardinia, Italy"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790175> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Radiometric correction (SAR) is a crucial preprocessing step for Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) data that aims to correct the intensity values of the radar signals to eliminate or reduce various distortions caused by factors such as sensor geometry, atmospheric conditions, and surface topography. The goal is to obtain accurate, consistent backscatter measurements that reflect the true surface properties."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790175> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790175> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Radiometric correction (SAR)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790176> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "https://rudigens.github.io/asf_seminar/terrain_correction.pdf"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790176> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790176> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " Terrian correction (SAR)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790177> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The CuSum (Cumulative Sum) change detection algorithm is a statistical method used to identify significant changes in time series data, often applied in remote sensing for detecting changes in land cover, vegetation, or environmental conditions. The CuSum method works by accumulating the difference between observed values and a reference value (such as a baseline or mean) over time. When the accumulated sum exceeds a predefined threshold, it indicates a significant change or shift in the data."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790177> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> " CuSum change detection algorithm"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790178> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/Resource> "https://www.politicheagricole.it/flex/cm/pages/ServeBLOB.php/L/IT/IDPagina/11131"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790178> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Italian Forest Service (CUFAA), or Corpo Unico Forestale dello Stato, is a governmental organization responsible for managing and protecting Italy's forests and natural resources. CUFAA oversees forest conservation, wildfire prevention, environmental protection, and the sustainable management of forest ecosystems. The service also plays a crucial role in monitoring forest health, combating illegal logging, and conducting research on forestry and biodiversity. Additionally, CUFAA supports disaster response efforts, particularly during forest fires, by using advanced technologies such as remote sensing for early detection and monitoring. The organization contributes to national and international environmental policies, promoting sustainable forestry practices."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790178> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
