<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R790183> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "Phenological Sequence Pattern (PSP) refers to the temporal patterns of seasonal changes in vegetation, including key stages such as bud burst, flowering, leaf expansion, senescence, and dormancy. These patterns are influenced by climate, environmental factors, and biological processes and can be observed and analyzed through time-series remote sensing data, particularly from satellites like Sentinel-2 or MODIS. PSP analysis helps to understand the seasonal dynamics of ecosystems, crop growth cycles, or forest phenology by tracking the timing and progression of these phases over time."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
