<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796006> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The GELU-tanh activation function is an approximation of the GELU (Gaussian Error Linear Unit) activation function using the tanh function, which is computationally less expensive than the Gaussian error function. The GELU-tanh function retains the smoothness and performance benefits of the original GELU function while being more efficient to compute."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
