<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796027> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Stack training dataset consists of 6 trillion tokens of source code from over 300 programming languages. \u200B It is useful for developing code-centric AI applications, providing a rich and diverse collection of programming language data. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stack"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796028> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The UltraChat training dataset is comprised of approximately 1.4M dialogues generated by ChatGPT, covering a wide range of topics, with a subset version called \"UltraChat 200k\" containing a heavily filtered selection of 200k dialogues used for faster fine-tuning purposes. It is used to train powerful language models with general conversational capabilities."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "UltraChat"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796029> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The OSS-Instruct training dataset typically consists of around 75k entries, used to train LLMs/SLMs specifically for code generation by leveraging open-source code snippets to generate high-quality instruction data through a technique called \"OSS-Instruct\". This method helps mitigate bias in instruction generation by drawing from diverse real-world code examples."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "OssInstruct"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796030> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The dataset consists of approximately 70k instruction-response pairs, used to fine-tune LLMs/SLMs, enabling them to follow diverse and complex instructions with high-quality responses. The dataset is curated from a combination of existing instruction-based datasets, with additional human-generated prompts and responses designed to push the model's capabilities, allowing to handle complex instructions and generate more creative and informative responses."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EvolInstruct"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796031> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The MiniCPM small language model, released in April 2024, is a pre-trained model available in 1.2 billion and 2.4 billion parameter versions, trained on diverse datasets including Dolma, C4, Pile, Stack, StarCoder, UltraChat, OssInstruct, and EvolInstruct, using a Warmup-Stable-Decay (WSD) learning rate scheduler. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
