<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796039> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The SlimPajama training dataset consists of 627 billion tokens. \u200B It is a cleaned and deduplicated version of the RedPajama dataset, designed to provide high-quality and diverse text for training language models. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796039> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796039> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SlimPajama"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796040> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The TinyLlama small language model, released in January 2024, is a 1 billion parameter pre-trained model trained on the SlimPajama and StarCoder datasets, utilizing Grouped Query Attention (GQA), SiLU activation, Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP), Flash Attention, and xFormers for enhanced efficiency."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TinyLlama"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796041> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Flash Attention mechanism accelerates the self-attention process by minimizing memory overhead and optimizing computation, allowing models to process longer sequences more efficiently by reducing the need for storing intermediate results and leveraging efficient memory access patterns. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796041> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796041> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796041> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Flash Attention"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796042> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP) training technique involves distributing both the model parameters and optimizer states across multiple devices to maximize memory efficiency and parallelism during training. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796042> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796042> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796043> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The xFormers training technique involves using a modular and efficient library designed to optimize and accelerate the training of Transformer models by implementing various memory and computational efficiency improvements. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796043> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796043> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "xFormers"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
