<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796059> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/hasContent> "[Game theory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_theory) is a branch of applied mathematics that provides tools for analyzing situations in which parties, called players, make decisions. Its development started during WWII, and since then, the Game Theory has been a part of Operations Research. Its methods have found their implementation in modern applied science. The following comparison was created from the review paper on the implementation of [Game Theory in Cyber Security](https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4336/15/4/28).  When a player has no strategic interest in the outcome, the game is referred to as a 'Game with Nature'. In the context of decision-making, this scenario is known as decision-making under uncertainty. "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796059> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
