<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796093> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The OpenELM small language model, released in April 2024, is available in 270 million, 450 million, 1.1 billion, and 3 billion parameter versions, pre-trained on datasets like RefinedWeb, deduplicated PILE, a subset of RedPajama, and Dolma v1.6, and features GQA, SwiGLU, RoPE, RMSNorm, and LLaMA-style tokenization for enhanced performance."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
