<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796187> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The GELU (Gaussian Error Linear Unit) activation function is defined as: GELU(x) = x * \u03A6(x) \u200Bwhere \u03A6(x) is the standard Gaussian cumulative distribution function (CDF).\u200B \u200BThe GELU activation function is smoother than ReLU and is widely used in models such as BERT and GPT for better gradient flow control. It effectively combines the input with the Gaussian error function, enhancing the model's performance."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
