<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796257> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "MUFFIN, a new scheme of instruction-following dataset curation. Specifically, it automatically Scales Tasks per Input by diversifying  tasks with various input facets. Experimental results across four zero-shot benchmarks, spanning both Scaling-Inputs and Scaling Input-Free Tasks schemes, reveal that LLMs/SLMs, at various scales, trained on MUFFIN generally demonstrate superior instruction-following capabilities."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796257> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796257> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Muffin"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796258> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The T0-SF (T0 Supervised Fine-tuning) training dataset is designed to enhance the instruction-following capabilities of LLMs/SLMs. It consists of a diverse set of instructions and corresponding responses."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796258> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796258> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "T0-SF"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796259> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The SNI (Super-Natural Instructions) training dataset is designed to enhance the instruction-following capabilities of LLMs/SLMs. It consists of a diverse set of instructions and corresponding responses. Each example in the dataset includes an instruction or prompt, followed by a detailed response that the model is expected to generate. \u200B The instructions cover a wide range of tasks and domains, providing the model with varied examples to learn from. \u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796259> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796259> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SNI"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796260> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The CoT (Chain-of-Thought) training dataset is designed to enhance the reasoning capabilities of language models by providing them with examples that require step-by-step logical reasoning. \u200B The CoT Collection is an instruction-tuning dataset that augments 1.88M CoT rationales across 1,060 tasks. The CoT dataset consists of problems and questions that require multi-step reasoning to arrive at the correct answer. Each example in the dataset includes a question or problem statement, followed by a detailed step-by-step solution that outlines the logical reasoning process needed to solve the problem."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796260> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796260> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CoT"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796261> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "The FlanT5 small language model, released in October 2022, is an instruction-tuned model with parameter sizes of 80 million, 250 million, 780 million, and 3 billion, trained on datasets including Muffin, T0-SF, SNI, and CoT.\u200B\u200B"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R796261> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/C15002> .
