<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R801685> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/description> "A wind turbine is a device that converts kinetic energy from the wind into electrical energy. To be useful in studies, their design properties used in calculations should be known. The following table provides a list of wind turbines studied in Cameroon as potential wind turbines for electricity generation. Their characteristics includes:\n-The hub height, at which wind speed measurements are taken.\n-The rotor diameter which defines the area swept by the blades, and thus influences the energy captured or power produced.\n-The rated power representing the maximum power a turbine is designed to produce.\n-The cut-in speed, the minimum speed required to generate electricity.\n-The rated speed, being the speed at which the turbine reaches the maximum power output.\n-The cut-off speed, the maximum speed at which it is designed to run safely.\n "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
