<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8280> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P14> "This ontology is used to describe people and social relationship on the Web. It is mostly focused on people's existence in the virtual world, with many properties related to online activity or identity: foaf:mbox, foaf:skypeID, foaf:msnID, foaf:geekcode, etc. Nothing about family relations, physical address... It provides similar information on organisations or groups with a similar focus on their existence on the Web (work place webpage, etc). It is particularly well suited for describing people on Web-based Social platforms (facebook, twitter, blogspot, ...)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
