<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8422> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8422> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "following the gradual adjustment of the top-chamber CO2 concentration to the reference CO2 concentration, the RS and its \u03B413C stabilised after about 3 h to values for RS of 0.45 g CO2 m\u22122 h\u22121, \u03B413CRs of \u221228.5 \u00B1 0.3\u2030 and Dc of 8.4 \u00B1 0.4 mm2 s\u22121 (mean \u00B1 SD, n measurements = 60)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8423> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8423> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "the \u03B413C of CO2 respired from roots, litter/humus, and SOM during incubations of samples collected at San Rossore stabilized after about 10 min. After stabilization, \u03B413CSOM was more 13C-enriched (\u221222.2 \u00B1 0.5\u2030, mean \u00B1 SE) than \u03B413CL (\u221228.3 \u00B1 1\u2030) and \u03B413CR (\u221230.3 \u00B1 0.5\u2030). Among the three end-members, only \u03B413CSOM showed a significant difference between morning and afternoon by about \u22121\u2030 (P = 0.02). In addition, the \u03B413C of root tissues, litter/humus, and SOM collected at the field site were \u221227.9 \u00B1 0.14\u2030, \u221227.3 \u00B1 0.41\u2030 and \u221225.2 \u00B1 0.73\u2030 respectively."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
