<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8428> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Measurements taken by the Cassini spacecraft inside the plume released by the south polar regions of Saturn's moon Enceladus"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8429> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8429> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "the Cassini spacecraft flew close by the moon Enceladus 14 times"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8430> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8430> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "the Cassini spacecraft sometimes flew as low as 25 km above the surface of the moon Enceladus and directly through the plume"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8431> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P7037> <http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8432> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8431> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8431> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "partially/fully connected to the flux tube connecting the Enceladus moon with Cassini"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8432> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8432> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Features in the data can be interpreted as that the spacecraft was connected to the plume material along field lines well before entering the high density region of the plume. Sharp absorption signatures as the result of losses of energetic electrons bouncing along those field lines, through the emitted gas and dust clouds, clearly depend on flyby geometry as well as on measured pitch angle/look direction of the instrument. We found that the depletion signatures during some of the flybys show \u201Cramp-like\u201D features where only a partial depletion has been observed further away from the moon followed by nearly full absorption of electrons closer in."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8433> <http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P7072> <http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8434> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/resource/R8433> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Resource> .
